mali-fbdev: do not close fd 0 after a failed ION allocation

The window data is calloc()ed, so every surface starts with dmabuf_fd 0.
When the ION allocation fails (seen on the RG35XX-H after a long suspend:
ION_IOC_ALLOC returns EPERM, "platform cma: Fail to allocate buffer"),
MALI_EGL_DeinitPixmapSurfaces() treats those surfaces as allocated and
close()s fd 0. DraStic then opens the ROM as fd 0 and reports "could not
find entry in file" for every game. Mark the surfaces as unallocated.

diff --git a/src/video/mali-fbdev/SDL_malivideo.c b/src/video/mali-fbdev/SDL_malivideo.c
index 5fe9db6..5ceb22b 100644
--- a/src/video/mali-fbdev/SDL_malivideo.c
+++ b/src/video/mali-fbdev/SDL_malivideo.c
@@ -430,6 +430,11 @@ MALI_CreateWindow(_THIS, SDL_Window * window)
     /* Setup driver data for this window */
     window->driverdata = windowdata;
 
+    /* No ION buffer yet: a failed setup must not make the teardown close fd 0 */
+    for (int i = 0; i < SDL_arraysize(windowdata->surface); i++) {
+        windowdata->surface[i].dmabuf_fd = -1;
+    }
+
     /* Use the entire screen when the blitter isn't enabled or the selected
        resolution doesn't make any sense. */
     if ((displaydata->blitter == NULL) || (window->w < 32 || window->h < 32)) {
